# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io).
#
# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository"), Zenodo and reference managers, so a citation can
# be picked up without anyone retyping it.
#
# The DOI is the Zenodo archive of every MadY version. The app shows the same author, year,
# version and DOI through `citation()` in `apps/desktop/src/renderer/src/shell/AboutPane.tsx`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MadY
message: >-
  If MadY was useful in work you publish, a citation is appreciated. It is a
  request, not a condition of the licence — and it says nothing about your
  figures, which are yours entirely.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Elias
    given-names: Mikael
abstract: >-
  A scientific graphing and statistics desktop application: a fully editable
  vector document model with a validated statistics engine, built to run
  entirely offline.
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.6.1
date-released: "2026-10-06"
